      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Tailscale didn't stop the Hugging Face intrusion",
      "url": "https://tailscale.com/blog/hugging-face-intrusion",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49127306",
      "score": 566,
      "comments": 211,
      "author": "bluehatbrit",
      "published": "2026-07-31T19:03:45Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Network-level Zero Trust tools like Tailscale cannot prevent application-layer breaches caused by compromised API keys or stolen OAuth tokens.",
        "AI platforms like Hugging Face require strict token rotation, short-lived credentials, and granular scoping to mitigate exposed model and dataset secrets.",
        "Defense-in-depth for ML pipelines must prioritize secret scanning, app-layer identity verification, and runtime isolation over basic perimeter controls."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "rss",
      "subsource": "github.blog",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Don’t stop early: Case-folding source code at memory speed",
      "url": "https://github.blog/engineering/architecture-optimization/dont-stop-early-case-folding-source-code-at-memory-speed/",
      "discuss_url": "https://github.blog/engineering/architecture-optimization/dont-stop-early-case-folding-source-code-at-memory-speed/",
      "score": null,
      "comments": null,
      "author": "Alexander Neubeck",
      "published": "2026-07-31T16:00:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "GitHub achieved >45 GiB/s case-folding throughput on a single CPU core, matching main memory bandwidth for code search.",
        "Using branch-free loops and byte-space arithmetic eliminates branch mispredictions when normalizing ASCII characters at scale.",
        "Avoiding early-exit conditionals permits uniform execution, fully saturating CPU pipelines for high-volume text ingestion."
      ]
    },
